hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1","Abu Yaqoub Yusuf bin Wadh Al-Hashimi told us, Al-Mu’tamir bin Sulayman told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Yahya bin Yamar, he said: I said: What is meant by Abdullah bin Omar: O Abu Abdul Rahman, there are people who claim that there is no destiny. He said: Do we have any of them? I said: No. He said: Then inform them about me when you meet them, and that Ibn Umar has disavowed you before God, and you are disavowed of him. Then he said: Tell me. Omar Ibn Al-Khattab said: While we were sitting with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, among people, a man came who was not well-travelled, and who was not From the people of the country he passed until he came, then he sat in front of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Muhammad, what is Islam? He said: “Islam is that you bear witness that there is no god but God, and that Muhammad is the Messenger of God, and that you perform prayer, pay zakat, and perform Hajj to the House and perform Umrah. And she should take a bath after ritual impurity, complete the ablution, and fast during Ramadan.” He said: “If I do that, am I a Muslim?” He said: “Yes.” He said: You are right. He mentioned the hadith at length in asking about faith, charity, and the Hour."
